          {
            "arabic_text": "عَنْهُ عَنْ إِبْرَاهِيمَ عَنِ النَّوْفَلِيِّ عَنِ السَّكُونِيِّ عَنْ جَعْفَرٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلَامُ:",
            "chunk_type": "isnad",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "From him, from Ibrahim, from al-Nawfali, from al-Sakuni, from Ja'far, from his father, peace be upon them:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 13,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "arabic_text": "أَنَّ رَجُلًا شَرَدَ لَهُ بَعِيرَانِ فَأَخَذَهُمَا رَجُلٌ فَقَرَنَهُمَا فِي حَبْلٍ، فَاخْتَنَقَ أَحَدُهُمَا وَمَاتَ، فَرُفِعَ ذَلِكَ إِلَى عَلِيٍّ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ، فَلَمْ يُضَمِّنْهُ، وَقَالَ: «إِنَّمَا أَرَادَ الْإِصْلَاحَ».",
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "A man had two camels that ran off, so another man took them and tied them together with a rope. One of them was strangled and died. The matter was referred to Ali عليه السلام, and he did not hold him liable, and he said: “He only intended to set things right.”",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
